        summary: "On {DATE}, {V}, 18, was found dead in a pickup in a parking lot, poisoned by exhaust fumes. {V} had battled depression for years. Hundreds of texts from {D}, {V}'s partner, urged {V.him} to go through with it and said {D.he} would help. A call between them lasted forty minutes that night. {DL} says the messages were a lashing out after a fight and {D.he} did not think {V.he} would act.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Text Messages", "Hundreds of messages urging {V} to go through with it."), E(.digital, 3, "Call Log", "A forty-minute call that night."), E(.forensic, 2, "Medical Examiner", "Death by exhaust poisoning.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Venting", "{DL} says the texts were anger after a fight.")],
        role: "Detective who recovered the messages",
        exam: [.direct("What did you recover from {D}'s phone?", "\"Hundreds of text messages to {V}, many of them urging {V} to go through with it and saying {D} would help.\""), .direct("What did the messages say?", "\"Go through with it. The same message and variations of it ran across days, and they grew more frequent in the final weeks.\""), .direct("When was the last message?", "\"About an hour before {V}'s death. It was among the more direct messages in the whole thread.\""), .direct("What does the call log show?", "\"A forty-minute call between {D} and {V} on the night {V} died, ending before the last messages were sent.\""), .direct("What did {V} say in earlier messages?", "\"{V} often talked about a plan to end it all. {V} was 18 and had battled depression for years.\""), .direct("Did {D} call 911 or anyone for help?", "\"No. We found no call to 911, to {V}'s family, or to anyone who could have stepped in that night.\""), .cross("Did {D} write other kinds of messages too?", "\"Yes. Many were affectionate or ordinary, and the thread covers months of a close relationship.\""), .cross("Did {V} also write things that worried {D}?", "\"Often. {V} repeatedly mentioned a plan, and {D} was reacting to a long stretch of that.\""), .cross("Was there a fight that week?", "\"Yes. The messages show a bitter argument in the days before, and the harsh texts rise out of that.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything to suggest {D} thought {V} would act?", "\"Not in the messages I read. Several lines say {D} did not believe {V} would go through with it.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate with your investigation?", "\"Yes. {D} handed over the phone, answered questions, and wept through most of the interview.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pushed {V} to end {V.his} life.", "A cruel fight that {D} never meant to be taken seriously."),
        allocution: "\"I hurt someone who didn't deserve it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} told {V} to do it and asked for proof.", "{DL} deleted messages afterward."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you mean what you wrote?", "\"No. I wrote those messages in anger after a terrible fight. I wanted to hurt {V} back, and I did not mean them.\""), .direct("How long had you and {V} been together?", "\"About two years. {V} struggled with depression the whole time, and I tried to help.\""), .direct("What was the call that night about?", "\"We argued and then calmed down. We talked for forty minutes, and I thought it ended on a better note.\""), .direct("Did you think {V} would act?", "\"No. {V} had said it many times, and nothing ever came of it. I did not think this time was any different.\""), .direct("What did you do after the call?", "\"I went to sleep. I woke up to a message from {V}'s family, and I could not believe it.\""), .direct("What do you want {V}'s family to know?", "\"I am so sorry. I loved {V}. I said terrible things I cannot take back, and I will live with it.\""), .cross("You urged {V} to go through with it, didn't you?", "\"In anger, yes. I wrote it, and I wish I could erase every word.\""), .cross("You said you would help, didn't you?", "\"I did not mean it. It was a cruel thing to say.\""), .cross("You did not call 911, did you?", "\"No. I did not know there was anything to call about. I thought it was another bad night.\""), .cross("{V} had told you about a plan many times, hadn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. And every time nothing happened. That is why I stopped taking it seriously.\""), .cross("You knew {V} was fragile, didn't you?", "\"I did. That makes what I wrote worse, and I know it.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, 18, was found dead in a pickup in a parking lot, poisoned by exhaust fumes. Hundreds of texts from {D}, {V}'s partner, urged {V.him} to go through with it and said {D.he} would help, and a forty-minute call ended that night.", "{D} lashed out in anger after a fight and never thought {V} would act. Cruel words from someone who was hurting are a tragedy, not an intent to cause a death."),
        closings: ("Hundreds of messages urging {V} to go through with it, a forty-minute call, and no call for help. {V} was told to die, and {V} died.", "Angry words after a fight, from someone who did not believe {V} would act. The State must prove {D} intended {V}'s death, and anger is not intent."),
        timeline: [(-1, "A fight."), (0, "The messages."), (0, "The forty-minute call."), (1, "{V} is found.")],
        identified: "Recovered texts.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .female, "V": .male])

