        openings: ("Two weeks after a hurricane tore roofs off houses, {D} arrived in a truck with a magnetic sign claiming federal approval and collected deposits from dozens of homeowners, including $9,000 from {V}, 77. No work was done, and deposits passed $100,000.", "{D}'s contractor license was in process, and supply shortages caused delays after the storm. Overpromising in a disaster is a failure to deliver, not a plan to steal."),
