        theory: ("{D} deleted video that would show a use of force.", "A camera glitch."),
        allocution: "\"I let things get out of hand.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} knew of the complaint before the delete.", "The camera was never reported faulty."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you delete the footage?", "\"No. I did not delete it. I did not touch that file, and I did not know it was needed.\""), .direct("Why does the log show your log-in?", "\"It is shared. Several of us use the same account at the station, and I did not delete anything with it.\""), .direct("When did you hear about the complaint?", "\"Later. I heard about it after the footage was gone, and I did not know about it when the file vanished.\""), .direct("Where is the log-in used?", "\"At the station, on the shared computer in the squad room. Anyone on shift can sit down and use it.\""), .direct("What do you think happened to the file?", "\"The camera was glitchy and the file deleted itself. I have seen files vanish from that system before.\""), .direct("What do you want the lieutenant to know?", "\"I did not hide anything. I wanted the footage to exist, because it would have shown the truth.\""), .cross("The delete came from your log-in, didn't it?", "\"From the shared log-in. I did not type it.\""), .cross("You are the camera's assigned officer, aren't you?", "\"Yes. That is why I know the camera had problems.\""), .cross("Policy says footage may not be deleted for a year, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I know the policy, and I would never have broken it.\""), .cross("No backup was made, was it?", "\"No. I did not know a backup was needed until the complaint.\""), .cross("You did not report the glitch, did you?", "\"I mentioned it informally. I did not file a ticket, and that was a mistake.\"")],
