        role: "Drug task force agent",
        exam: [.direct("Please describe your work with the drug task force.", "\"I investigate overdose deaths and trace pills to their sources. I review messages and payment apps, and I work with medical examiners and labs.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"{V}, who was 24 and a nursing student, was found unresponsive in a rented room on {DATE} after taking a blue pill bought two nights earlier.\""), .direct("What did the medical examiner find?", "\"Fentanyl toxicity caused the death. The level was enough to cause death, and no other cause explained it.\""), .direct("What did the payment app messages show?", "\"{V} asked {D} for two of the blues and sent $40. {D} was a shift lead at the warehouse where {V} worked part time.\""), .direct("What was found in {D}'s locker?", "\"A bag of matching blue pills. The pill analysis found fentanyl in the pills.\""), .direct("What did you learn about other coworkers?", "\"A coworker chat shows others also asked for pills. {D} sold pills to several coworkers.\""), .cross("Did {D} say what the pills were?", "\"{D} says {D} believed they were ordinary pain medicine. I cannot say what {D} knew.\""), .cross("What did {D} tell a coworker?", "\"{D} said the pills were strong and to take only half. That suggests {D} knew they were powerful.\""), .cross("How much did {D} pay for the pills?", "\"$8 each in bulk. {D} sold them for $20 each. {D} made a profit, even if a small one.\""), .cross("Did {V} take only one pill?", "\"{V} took a blue pill two nights before. We do not know if {V} took more, or what else {V} took.\""), .cross("Could the pills have been pressed with fentanyl without {D} knowing?", "\"Yes. Counterfeit pills are often pressed without the seller knowing. I cannot say what {D} knew.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold a fentanyl pill that killed a coworker.", "A coworker who passed along pills at cost."),
